---
import InfoLayout from '../../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const updated = '2026-09-28';
---

<InfoLayout
  title="Disclaimer | Infinite Calculators"
  description="Results from Infinite Calculators are estimates for information only, not financial, legal, medical or religious advice. Read the limits of each tool."
  h1="Disclaimer"
  updated={updated}
>
  <p>
    Every calculator on {site.name} gives an estimate based on the values you enter and the method
    explained on its page. We test each one against known answers, but mistakes are possible and your
    situation may differ from the assumptions a calculator makes. Please check any result that matters
    before you act on it.
  </p>

  <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Results are for general information only. They are not financial, tax, legal, medical, engineering or
    religious advice, and they are not religious rulings (fatwas or other formal opinions).
  </p>

  <h2>Money and tax</h2>
  <p>
    Tax rates change, and many US cities and counties add their own sales tax on top of the state rate.
    Where a calculator uses published rates, the page shows the date they were last checked. Confirm
    rates with the relevant tax authority, and speak to a qualified adviser about your own finances.
  </p>

  <h2>Home and building projects</h2>
  <p>
    Material estimates assume the shapes and sizes you enter. Real jobs need extra for waste, uneven
    ground, spillage and surface texture. Follow local building codes and your supplier's advice, and
    consult a professional for structural work.
  </p>

  <h2>School grades</h2>
  <p>
    Schools and teachers weight and round grades in different ways. Your syllabus or instructor has the
    final word on how your grade is calculated.
  </p>

  <h2>Religious calculators</h2>
  <p>
    Religious calculations depend on methods and schools of thought that differ between communities. Each
    page states the method it uses. In particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Zakat:</strong> results are a guide only. Please consult a qualified scholar about your own
      zakat, especially for business assets, debts, retirement funds and jewelry.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hijri dates:</strong> converted dates follow the Umm al-Qura calendar. Local moon sighting can
      make the actual date one day earlier or later.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Church calendars:</strong> Easter dates follow the standard Western and Orthodox calculation
      methods. Your church's published calendar takes priority.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Dates and times</h2>
  <p>
    Date and time results use the calendar and clock settings of your own device. Daylight saving changes
    and time zones can affect results that span them, and each calculator page notes how it handles
    this.
  </p>

  <h2>Report an error</h2>
  <p>
    If you think a result is wrong, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> with the page, your inputs and
    the result you expected. We check every report.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
